fe** (~15,000 population): Known for very large, distinct, polygonal spots that cover a wider surface area. Average: ~100 spots each.\n- **Captive Giraffes** (~3,000 population, adjusted for mixed species): Average: ~140 spots each.\n\n3. **Calculation:**\n- Southern: 50,000 × 150 = 7,500,000\n- Masai: 45,000 × 120 = 5,400,000\n- Northern: 15,000 × 160 = 2,400,000\n- Reticulated: 15,000 × 100 = 1,500,000\n- Captive: 3,000 × 140 = 420,000\n\nTotal estimated spots = 7,500,000 + 5,400,000 + 2,400,000 + 1,500,000 + 420,000 = 17,220,000.\n\nBased on this objective biological and demographic breakdown, my single most accurate estimate is:\n\n**17,220,000**",
